See `docs/rules/01-architecture.md` for the full rule text — this file exists only so Cursor auto-loads it. Do not duplicate content here; edit the canonical `.md` file and this pointer stays valid.

Key points: **two execution paths** — `local-worker` (localhost/dev servers/auth'd pages, stdio MCP) and the cloud path (`mcp-server` + `worker`, remote HTTP MCP). `mcp-server` is the only internet-facing deployable on the cloud path (no separate API gateway). Package boundaries are non-negotiable — `shared` has zero I/O, `mcp-server` never touches a browser, `worker` never speaks MCP/OAuth, `local-worker` never imports from `worker` or invokes the stealth ladder. `BrowserProvider` is the only sanctioned Patchright touchpoint. Tools stay separate, never collapsed into a `mode` flag; a fifth motion-capture tool is planned and pre-justified.
